/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL003-M2 ARM D -- kOmegaSST.  "Try other models" (Sanaa 2026-08-25).

  THIS ARM CARRIES A DECLARED COUPLED CHANGE, NOT A SINGLE-KEYWORD SWAP, and it
  is included DESPITE that precisely because dropping the model most able to
  move wall friction would be answer-directed (PREREGISTRATION_DRAFT.md
  section 3, 4).  kOmegaSST transports (k, omega) rather than (k, epsilon), so
  changing to it necessarily also changes:
    - the second turbulence field: 0/omega replaces 0/epsilon;
    - system/fvSchemes: div(phi,omega) replaces div(phi,epsilon);
    - system/fvSolution: the solved-variable class "(U|k|omega)" and the omega
      relaxation factor replace their epsilon spellings.
  The wall treatment is kept as close to run 1 as the model allows: nut still
  uses nutkWallFunction and k still uses kqRWallFunction (0/nut, 0/k byte-
  identical to run 1); omega uses omegaWallFunction, which BLENDS the viscous-
  sublayer and log-law omega rather than switching, so the same numeric y+ floor
  is a conservative validity floor (PREREGISTRATION_DRAFT.md section 8).

  INLET omega IS DERIVED, NOT GUESSED, and is chosen to reproduce run 1's inlet
  turbulence STATE so ARM D is comparable to A/B/C: with beta* = Cmu = 0.09,
      omega_in = epsilon_in / (Cmu * k_in)
               = 16845.37817870935 / (0.09 * 9.375)
               = 19964.892656248117  1/s
  which returns epsilon_in exactly (Cmu*k*omega = 16845.37817870935).

  COEFFICIENTS.  kOmegaSST's default constant set (Menter 2003) is used as
  shipped in OpenFOAM v2606
  (src/TurbulenceModels/turbulenceModels/RAS/kOmegaSST); the model has a large
  blended coefficient set and is left at its documented library defaults rather
  than transcribed, with printCoeffs on so the run log records the set actually
  used.  This is the honest reading of "the standard SST model".
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      turbulenceProperties;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

simulationType  RAS;

RAS
{
    RASModel        kOmegaSST;
    turbulence      on;
    printCoeffs     on;
}

